<<<
M. in the phrase pass m. means an inspection; & to pass an inspection very fairly is quite a different thing from passing a very fair inspection. Pass m. is one of the many idioms that must be taken as they are or left alone.
===
*M.* in the phrase *pass m.* means an inspection; & to pass an inspection very fairly is quite a different thing from passing a very fair inspection. *Pass m.* is one of the many idioms that must be taken as they are or left alone.
>>>

